**How to implement.** `<name>.setup-json` holds a setup, replacing S4.3's scene file, and the constructor's scene save and load become CreateSetup and loading a setup (the S8.2 brief: '<name>.setup-json (schema + version) REPLACES S4.3's scene file shape. Scene.SceneSnapshot, and whatever only it used, is deleted; the constructor's scene save / load becomes setup save / load'; 001 §P `CreateSetup`; 001 §A 'Kit extensions … .setup-json'). The stack is step 146's (`nodeOf`, `JsonNode.canonicalFileText`, `CanonicalJson.parseVersionedText`, `SchemaValidation.validateWith`); no second parser or writer is written. Kit files of the old shape exist only under test output folders, so the schema version stays 1 and no reader of the old shape is kept (.spec-md §7: kit file shapes change in later parts and no migration is needed). Each doc is one to three lines citing spec 0050 S8.2. (1) Domain. (a) `Setups.fs` (step 256): `SetupFile = { schemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion; setup : Setup }`, the `.setup-json`, with `static member currentSchemaVersion : FileSchemaVersion` = 1; `type Setup with member this.setupFile : SetupFile` is the setup at the current version, a file being read back as its `setup` field (one direction, ELEV006). `Setup` gains `member this.libraryReferences : EntryReference list`: the `placement.valueId` of every slot that names a library entry (`ElementValueId.tryToLibraryEntryId`, step 24) as an `EntryLatestReference`, over the current slots and then each history record's, in slot order, each once: the rule of step 147's `SceneSnapshot.libraryReferences`, moved here, because every revision an experiment may reference needs its entries in the kit. (b) `OpticalConstructor.Domain/Scene.fs`: `SceneStoreError`, `SceneName`, `SceneElement`, `SceneSnapshot` and `SceneFile` (`Scene.fs:SceneName`, `:SceneElement`, `:SceneSnapshot`, steps 147 and 151) are deleted with their members. `SnapMode` (`Scene.fs:SnapMode`) stays, because the window's `snapChain` holds it, and the module doc becomes one to three lines: the window's snap mode, which a setup does not carry (spec 0050 S8.2). The comment above `Scene.fs`'s `<Compile>` in `OpticalConstructor.Domain.fsproj` is cut to the words that stay true, naming no scene file, and nothing is added. A setup is the optical path: the table view, the snap mode and the rotation pivot that step 147's scene file held are the window's, so loading a setup leaves them as they are. (2) Storage. (a) `schema/setup.schema.json` (step 147) describes the setup file. `schemaVersion` is a positive integer, checked unconditionally; only under `if` it is 1 the root holds exactly `schemaVersion` and `setup`, and `setup` holds exactly `name` (a string holding a non-white-space character, the pattern `\S`), `revision` (a positive integer), `slots` (an array) and `history` (an array whose items hold exactly `revision`, a positive integer, and `slots`, an array). A slot's shape is bound by the serializer, which answers `MalformedJsonErr` for a malformed one. `SchemaValidation.validateSceneFile` (step 147) is renamed `validateSetupFile`, its schema still loaded once behind a `lazy`. (b) `KitContentFiles.fs`: `SceneFile.fileText` and `KitFileText.parseSceneFile` (step 147) become `SetupFile.fileText` and `KitFileText.parseSetupFile` over the same stack and `SetupKitFile.extension`. On the `KitProxy` extension (step 148), `writeScene`, `readScene` and `readSceneNames` are deleted and replaced by `member this.writeSetup (setup : Setup) : Result<unit, KitError>`, which writes `setup.setupFile.fileText` with `writeKindFile SetupKitFile setup.name.fileStem`, a rendering error being `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file, and `member this.readSetups () : Result<Setup list, KitError>`, which parses every stem `listKindFiles SetupKitFile` answers; a refusal, or a file whose setup's `name.fileStem` is not its own stem ignoring case, is `KitFileRejectedErr` naming the file and refuses the whole read, so a window never opens a kit with a setup left out; the answer is ordered by name (ordinal). On the `KitLibraryContext` extension (step 149), `recordScene` becomes `member this.recordSetup (setup : Setup) : Result<unit, KitLibraryError>`: `snapshotReferences setup.libraryReferences` (step 139), then `writeSetup`, a `KitError` being `KitLibraryKitErr`. Through `readOnlyView` (step 131) `writeSetup` answers `KitReadOnlyErr`. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/KitOpening.fs`: `OpenedKit.scenes : SceneName list` (step 150) becomes `setups : Setup list`, the kit's setups as read at open, in name order; `openedOver` (step 172) reads `readSetups ()` where it read `readSceneNames ()`, a refusal closing the kit as any failed read does; `withRebindings` keeps it. (4) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/TableAndElementRotationView.fs`. (a) The model: `sceneName` (step 153) becomes `setupName : ControlCaption`, the setup name being typed; `savedScenes` becomes `kitSetups : Setups.Setup list`, the kit's setups in name order as the window last read or wrote them; and the model gains `activeSetupOpt : Setups.Setup option`, the kit setup the table draws as last created or loaded, `None` while the table is not yet a setup of the kit; each with a one-line doc. `initWith` sets them to `ControlCaption ""`, `[]` and `None`. The private content function `loadKit` and `ReloadKitChanges` share (step 187 (4)) takes the setups in place of the scene names, sets `kitSetups`, and sets `activeSetupOpt` to the setup among them whose name is the active one's (`None` when there is none): `loadKit` passes `opened.setups`, `ReloadKitChanges` reads `readSetups ()` where it read `readSceneNames ()` (an error keeping the model and the offer with step 187's text), and `CopyChosenExperiments` (step 225) passes `model.kitSetups`. (b) Messages, each with a one-line doc: `SceneSetName` becomes `SetSetupName of ControlCaption`; `SceneSave` becomes `CreateSetup` (the table becomes a new setup of the kit, named by the field); `SceneLoad of SceneName` becomes `ActivateSetup of Kit.SetupName` (the kit's setup of that name is drawn on the table). (c) Arms. `SetSetupName name` sets `setupName`. `CreateSetup` is refused by the read-only guard of step 185 like `SceneSave` was; otherwise `SetupName.tryCreate model.setupName.value` (step 255) and then `Setup.create name (model.elements |> List.map (fun s -> s.recordedWith model.kitItems)) model.kitSetups` (steps 256, 258), either refusal setting `kitStatus` to `Not created — <e.describe>` and writing nothing; an `Ok setup` is recorded through `{ kit = model.kit; imports = model.catalogueImports }.recordSetup setup`: on `Ok` `kitSetups` holds it in name order, `activeSetupOpt` is `Some setup` and `kitStatus` is `Created setup '<name>'.`; on `Error e` nothing else changes and `kitStatus` is `Not saved to the kit — <e.describe>`. `ActivateSetup name`: the setup of that name in `kitSetups` makes `elements` its `slots` drawn through the kit's items (`slot.drawnWith model.kitItems`, step 258), `activeSetupOpt` that setup, `selection` `TableSelected`, `drag` `NotPressed`, `elementMenu` `None` (the resets `restoreScene` made) and `kitStatus` `Loaded setup '<name>'.`; with none, `kitStatus` is `Load failed — <describe>` of `UnknownSetupErr` naming the name and the table is left alone. It writes nothing, so a read-only kit loads setups. `captureScene` and `restoreScene` (step 259) are deleted: the table's elements are the setup's slots (step 259). (d) The view. `collectionBuilderView`'s scene row (step 153) becomes the setup row under the heading `Setup:`: the name `TextBox` carrying `ConstructorUiId.setupNameField`, dispatching `SetSetupName` on Enter and on lost focus, and the `workbenchButton` `Create setup` (`ConstructorUiId.createSetupButton`, dispatching `CreateSetup`, withheld under a read-only kit as Save scene was, step 185); then the `kitStatus` line; then, when `kitSetups` is not empty, `Saved setups:` and a `WrapPanel` named `ConstructorUiId.savedSetups` holding one `workbenchButton` per setup (`ConstructorUiId.savedSetup setup.name`, captioned by the name, dispatching `ActivateSetup`); then the inverse `Data files:` section. (5) Ids. `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`: `sceneNameField`, `saveSceneButton` and `savedScenes` (step 153) become `setupNameField` (`"SetupNameField"`), `createSetupButton` (`"CreateSetupButton"`) and `savedSetups` (`"SavedSetups"`) under a doc line naming the setup row. `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`: `savedScene` and the `SceneName.caption` extension (step 153) become `static member savedSetup (name : Kit.SetupName) : ConstructorUiId` (`SavedSetup_<name>`) and `type Kit.SetupName with member this.caption : ControlCaption`. No other message, field, id or option is added. Tests. (i) `KitContentFileJsonTests` (steps 146, 147): its fixture becomes a setup `Bench: A` at revision 2 whose slots are a light source bound to the 600 nm source preset (`PresetIds.source600`), a linear polarizer bound to the linear-polarizer preset holding a test-local item with `DialTurn (−20°)` and an unbound detector, with one history record at revision 1 whose polarizer holds nothing. `a scene is stored under its name made filesystem-safe` becomes `a setup is stored under its name made filesystem-safe` over `SetupName`, the same texts and stems. `a setup file round-trips through its canonical text`: the file of that setup round-trips equal through `fileText` and `parseSetupFile`, holds no `\r`, ends with one `\n`, lists its top-level keys `schemaVersion` then `setup`, and writes the same text again. `a setup file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`: `schemaVersion` 2, with the body and alone, answers `UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr` with `fileExtension = SetupKitFile.extension`. `a schema-invalid or malformed setup file is refused before it binds`: the text without `setup`, with `setup.name` `"   "`, with `setup` lacking `history`, with `setup.revision` 0 and with an extra top-level key answer `SchemaValidationErr`, and `{` `MalformedJsonErr`. `a scene references the library entries its elements bind, each once, at their latest` becomes `a setup references the library entries its slots bind in every revision, each once, at their latest`: the fixture's `libraryReferences` are exactly the `EntryLatestReference`s of the source and the linear-polarizer presets, in that order; a revision binding the source preset again references it once; a setup of unbound slots references nothing. (ii) `SceneRoundTripTests.fs` is renamed `SetupRoundTripTests.fs`, `module SetupRoundTripTests`, its `<Compile>` entry and the comment above it naming the setup file, in no more words. It keeps its fixture slots as a setup `Experiment A`. `a scene round-trips through its kit file, reproducing ids, kinds, placements, bindings and view state` becomes `a setup round-trips through its kit file, reproducing its slots, their items and its revisions`: `writeSetup` of it, then `readSetups` answers `[ that setup ]`, the folder holds `Experiment A.setup-json`, and a model whose `kitSetups` hold it, after `ActivateSetup`, has `elements` equal to its slots. `writing a scene again under its name replaces its kit file` becomes `writing a setup again under its name replaces its kit file`. `reading a scene the kit never held is MissingKitFileErr` becomes `a kit with no setup files reads no setups`: a fresh kit answers `Ok []`. `a setup file that does not read refuses the scene list, naming the file` becomes `a setup file that does not read, or holds another name, refuses the setup list, naming the file`: `Broken.setup-json` written as `{`, and `B.setup-json` holding `Experiment A`'s text, each make `readSetups` answer `KitFileRejectedErr` naming that file. `SceneName.tryCreate rejects a blank name as InvalidScene carrying a reason`, `SceneName.tryCreate rejects a null name as InvalidScene` and `SceneName.tryCreate accepts a non-blank name and round-trips its value` are deleted with `SceneName`; step 255's `a setup name keeps its text, refuses a blank one and takes its file stem from the shared name rule` covers the setup name. `SnapMode round-trips its wire form: true snaps to the beam, false is free placement` moves with the class unchanged. (iii) `KitLibraryTests` (step 149): `recording a scene snapshots the entries its elements bind` becomes `recording a setup snapshots the entries its slots bind in every revision, then writes its file`: a setup whose current slots bind the 600 nm source preset and the multilayer sample (`SampleIds.multilayerQwId`) by value id and whose history binds the glass plate (`SampleIds.glassPlate1mmId`), recorded through `recordSetup`, leaves `listSnapshots` holding the source, both samples at their latest versions, their materials and their categories, and `readSetups` answers the setup. (iv) `KitOpeningTests` (step 150): `opening a kit reads its experiments and scenes` becomes `opening a kit reads its experiments and setups`, a setup `Bench` written through `writeSetup` answering `setups` `[ Bench ]` when the kit is opened again. (v) `ExperimentCollectionRoundTripTests` (step 148): `a read-only kit refuses experiment and scene writes and writes nothing` becomes `a read-only kit refuses experiment and setup writes and writes nothing`, `writeSetup` answering `KitReadOnlyErr`. (vi) `KitWindowModelTests` (steps 185, 187): `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing` sends `SetSetupName (ControlCaption "Bench")` then `CreateSetup` where it sent the scene messages, with the same assertions over `kitSetups`; `Reload reads the kit's files in and clears the offer` has the other writer write a setup through `writeSetup`, and the reload leaves `kitSetups` holding it. (vii) New `OpticalConstructor.Tests/SetupModelTests.fs`, `module SetupModelTests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment; its model is `initMain ()` loaded through `loadKit` (step 152) of a kit folder under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, "SetupModelTests", <a new GUID>)` opened read-write through `KitOpening.openKitAt` (step 150) over the Built-in import context, as `KitWindowModelTests` opens its kits. `CreateSetup records the table as a new kit setup and makes it the active one`: with a linear polarizer added (`AddElement LinearPolarizer`), `SetSetupName (ControlCaption "Bench")` then `CreateSetup` leaves `kitSetups` `[ Bench ]` at revision 1 holding the table's slots, `activeSetupOpt` `Some Bench`, `kitStatus` `Created setup 'Bench'.`, the folder holding `Bench.setup-json` and the preset's snapshot under `library/`. `CreateSetup of a blank name, or of a name whose file the kit holds, is told and records nothing`: `"   "` and, after `Bench`, `"bench"` each set a `kitStatus` starting `Not created` and write no further setup file. `ActivateSetup draws the kit's setup on the table and keeps the window's view, snap mode and pivot`: after `Bench` is created, the polarizer removed (`RemoveSelectedElement`), the view zoomed, `SetRotationPivot PivotAtIncidentFace` sent, `ActivateSetup (SetupName "Bench")` puts the polarizer back with `Bench`'s slots, keeps the view, the snap mode and the pivot, and selects the table; `ActivateSetup (SetupName "nowhere")` sets a `kitStatus` starting `Load failed` and leaves `elements` as they were. (viii) `SceneSaveLoadTests.fs` is renamed `SetupSaveLoadTests.fs`, `module SetupSaveLoadTests`, its `<Compile>` entry following it. `a saved scene is a setup file in the kit and loads back onto the table` becomes `a created setup is a setup file in the kit and loads back onto the table` over `SetSetupName (ControlCaption "Bench: A")`, `CreateSetup`, `Bench_ A.setup-json`, the polarizer removed and `ActivateSetup`, and a model loaded from the same folder opened again lists `Bench: A`. `saving a scene with a blank name reports a typed status and writes nothing` becomes `creating a setup with a blank name, or one the kit holds, reports a typed status and writes nothing`: `"   "` and a second `Bench: A` each set a `kitStatus` starting `Not created` and write no further setup file. `loading a scene the kit does not hold reports a typed status and leaves the table alone` becomes `loading a setup the kit does not hold reports a typed status and leaves the table alone`. `the scene row renders its name field, Save scene and the saved scenes` (trait `ui-smoke`) becomes `the setup row renders its name field, Create setup and the saved setups`, holding `setupNameField`, `createSetupButton`, `savedSetups` and the setup's `savedSetup` button. (ix) `KitWindowTests` (step 185): `a read-only window withholds every write control` looks for `createSetupButton` where it looked for `saveSceneButton`. After this step `git grep -n -E "SceneSnapshot|SceneName|SceneFile|recordScene|readSceneNames" -- Berreman/` finds nothing.

**Acceptance.** After the setup file replaces the scene file, `<name>.setup-json` MUST hold a `Setup` read and written by `KitProxy.readSetups` / `writeSetup` and recorded with every revision's library snapshots by `KitLibraryContext.recordSetup`, `Scene.fs` MUST hold `SnapMode` alone, and `CreateSetup` / `ActivateSetup` MUST create the table as a kit setup and load one, `git grep -n -E "SceneSnapshot|SceneName|SceneFile|recordScene|readSceneNames" -- Berreman/` finding nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a setup is stored under its name made filesystem-safe`, `a setup file round-trips through its canonical text`, `a setup file of another schema version is UnsupportedSchemaVersionErr`, `a schema-invalid or malformed setup file is refused before it binds`, `a setup references the library entries its slots bind in every revision, each once, at their latest`, `a setup round-trips through its kit file, reproducing its slots, their items and its revisions`, `writing a setup again under its name replaces its kit file`, `a kit with no setup files reads no setups`, `a setup file that does not read, or holds another name, refuses the setup list, naming the file`, `SnapMode round-trips its wire form: true snaps to the beam, false is free placement`, `recording a setup snapshots the entries its slots bind in every revision, then writes its file`, `opening a kit reads its experiments and setups`, `a read-only kit refuses experiment and setup writes and writes nothing`, `a kit opened read-only refuses every write message and writes nothing`, `Reload reads the kit's files in and clears the offer`, `CreateSetup records the table as a new kit setup and makes it the active one`, `CreateSetup of a blank name, or of a name whose file the kit holds, is told and records nothing` and `ActivateSetup draws the kit's setup on the table and keeps the window's view, snap mode and pivot`, the count unchanged (three facts new, three deleted); ui-smoke MUST pass, including `the setup row renders its name field, Create setup and the saved setups`, its count unchanged; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `a created setup is a setup file in the kit and loads back onto the table`, `creating a setup with a blank name, or one the kit holds, reports a typed status and writes nothing`, `loading a setup the kit does not hold reports a typed status and leaves the table alone` and `a read-only window withholds every write control`, the count unchanged; and build, elevation and the fifteen s26 invariants MUST pass.
